    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d829">

                <pb facs="0978" n="966" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg966"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00114 Pacific War/151: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-03-01">March 1, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>505. American interests—Thailand. Your 1130, February 18th.<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d829-f1"/> Swiss Consulate, Bangkok, should be informed that United
                    States Government does not agree with statement that Geneva Prisoners of War
                    Convention is inapplicable in Thailand, as Thai Government is a party to the
                    Convention and as Japanese Government has agreed to apply its provisions.<anchor
                        n="17" xml:id="d829-f2"/>
                </p>
                <pb facs="0979" n="967" xml:id="pg967"/>
                <p>Request Swiss Minister, Tokyo, to bring this matter to the attention of the
                    Japanese authorities and to insist that the Japanese military forces in Thailand
                    apply the provisions of the Geneva Convention to American prisoners of war held
                    by them.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d829-f1" n="16" xml:id="d829-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it reported the views of the Thai Foreign Office concerning an
                    American aviator shot down in Thailand and made prisoner by Japanese forces.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d829-f2" n="17" xml:id="d829-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 503, March 1, to the Minister in Switzerland, the Department
                    requested that the Swiss Consul in Thailand remind the Bangkok authorities of
                    their obligations under the Geneva Convention in connection with an American
                    aviator arrested by Thai authorities (390.1115/6467).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
